diff --git a/docs/reference/api.md b/docs/reference/api.md
index 8a4df18..7f24f5c 100644
--- a/docs/reference/api.md
+++ b/docs/reference/api.md
@@ -738,4 +738,6 @@ released. The release steps are recorded in order-service's transactional outbox
 cancellation and delivered with retries (since 2026-11-17); wallet amounts go through their own
 durable retry table.
 
+**Per-shipment cancel.** A seller (`POST /api/seller/shipments/{id}/cancel`, own shipments only, 404 otherwise, 403 without an approved seller account) or an admin (`POST /api/admin/orders/{id}/shipments/{shipmentId}/cancel`, 404 if the shipment is not on that order) cancels one shipment with a `{reason}` body while it is still PLACED, CONFIRMED or PACKED (409 `ORDER_NOT_CANCELLABLE` later, 409 `INVALID_STATUS_TRANSITION` for an unpaid order or one on risk hold). Its pro-rata share of the paid items (the last shipment takes the remainder, and the shipping fee once) is refunded: the card part first, and a refund payment-service refuses or cannot be reached for returns 503 with nothing changed and can be retried; the wallet part is queued durably and never fails the call. A replay returns 200 with no second refund. While a cancel is in progress the shipment cannot be shipped (409 `RESOURCE_CONFLICT`). A whole-order cancel of a paid order is the cancel of every live shipment, so earlier partial cancels are never refunded again. `/status` with `CANCELLED` stays a 409.
+
 **Return refunds.** `POST /api/admin/returns/{id}/status` with `REFUNDED` (ADMIN or FINANCE) refunds a PICKED_UP return. The return response carries `shippingRefund` (the shipping fee included in `refundAmount`; non-zero only on the one return that completes the whole order, even when earlier returns covered other shipments) and `refundState` (null, `PENDING`, `SUCCEEDED` or `FAILED`: the state of the non-wallet leg). The wallet share is credited first and recorded; the rest goes to the card, or to the wallet for cash on delivery or `refundTo=WALLET`. A card refund payment-service has accepted but not confirmed leaves the return PICKED_UP with `refundState=PENDING`; a background job finishes it when the refund settles (`ORDER_RETURNS_REFUND_POLL_INTERVAL_MS`). The return becomes REFUNDED, stock is released and `RETURN_REFUNDED` is published only after the money has settled. Retrying is safe: an already REFUNDED return makes no payment call, and a second concurrent call gets 409 `RESOURCE_CONFLICT` (refund in progress). A cash-on-delivery refund that payment-service rejects (409 payment not collected, 404 no payment row) is returned as is and leaves the return PICKED_UP; nothing is credited outside payment-service.
